# `PluginContributions`

<SymbolMeta />

`PluginContributions` is supplied to one effective plugin during `Plugin::contribute`. It attaches that plugin's identity to every component, provider, and configuration binding it collects.

<SymbolSignature />

## Contract

Use `component` for a type with a static `ComponentDescriptor`, `component_descriptor` for a raw descriptor, `provider` for a trait-provider descriptor, and `config` for a `ConfigProperties` binding. Every call needs a distinct, stable `ContributionId` owned by the plugin's namespace. The collector records provenance before later registry validation, so a valid ID does not bypass descriptor or dependency validation.

The collector rejects duplicate contributor-local IDs and third-party IDs in the reserved `upwell/` namespace when it is finalized. With the `tooling` feature, `tooling` exposes a separate owner-scoped metadata collector; do not use app-neutral contribution IDs as a substitute for tooling resource identities.

Use [`contribute!`](/docs/latest/symbols/upwell_app/contribute) for literal declarative emissions, and use the [plugin workflow](/docs/latest/framework/extensions/plugins#preserve-provenance-while-contributing) when control flow requires the direct methods.

<SymbolMembers />
